  "description": "The 202B cross-signed attestation: version(1) || node_pubkey(32) || transport_id(1; 0x01 = nostr-secp256k1) || transport_key(32) || expiry_epoch(LE u64, mesh-epoch) || node_sig(64) || transport_sig(64). node_sig covers '111/attest-node/v1' || version || node_pubkey || transport_key || transport_id || expiry_epoch (NOTE: transport_key BEFORE transport_id - differs from the wire order); transport_sig covers '111/attest-transport/v1' || node_pubkey and is OPAQUE bytes to id111 (secp256k1/BIP340 verification is Layer 7's, behind the TransportVerifier seam; the KAT carries a fixed placeholder 0xa0..0xdf). Per section 14 these vectors cover encoding + signature verification only: expiry SEMANTICS are untestable until the mesh-epoch source lands (section 15) - the expiry cases here pin only the stored-and-compared ordering (a caller-supplied epoch, dead at current >= expiry_epoch). Supersedure: per (node_pubkey, transport_id) the greatest expiry_epoch wins; re-publication of a superseded attestation is rejected. 'expect' tokens: ok | err:length:<n> | err:version:<v> | err:tid:<b> | err:node-sig:<VerifyError> | err:transport-sig | err:expired:<expiry>:<current> | err:superseded:<retained>:<offered> | err:conflict:<epoch> | ok:pinned | ok:supersedes:<previous> | ok:duplicate. Epochs are decimal strings (u64).",
